 "poem": "183, The Commencement of the Composition of\nI. Adieu! Some Maidens have ago,\nTheir rose-lit cheeks and languid eyes because\n(To wear a happier mistress so\nWorthy, I grant you) let me speak again:\nIf left alone by Nature's self alone,\nOr any creature but the human brain,\nFor me with all that is true, you only,\nAnd not to charm me in your beauty,\nThe happiest act was once begun:\nIn former days, when in union liberty,\nUncheated passions and free passion,",
